      "writtenOn": "2022-11-16T11:50:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Separate CL works for me, thanks!\n\nAbout the zeroing, not sure which one\u0027s faster -- pkvm uses a fixmap in hyp_zero_page(), so we need to go through a whole map/unmap cycle with tlb inval etc. Not sure in which context is the guest when it issues the hypercall? Is it a preemptible section from the guest PoV? Even if that is the case, it\u0027s still preemptible by the host, which is a plus, so I\u0027d be inclined to leave that to the guest if possible.\n\nAnother idea (I promise I stop after this one :-)):\n - for protected guests, we make __pkvm_guest_relinquish_to_host() call a proper pkvm_guest_donate_host() function which implements all the usual machinery for memory transition in pKVM;\n - for non-protected guests, we make the relinquish hcall just return to the host which can then issue an __pkvm_host_unshare_guest() hypercall, which again goes through the normal machinery.\n \nIt\u0027s a bit cleaner conceptually, but also a bit slower. Wdyt?",
